    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the core change:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN` = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of existing owners in that same city (via `findAll()` filtered by city, case-insensitively). Since it runs before the owner is saved, the count excludes the owner being created \u2014 so two owners in the same city get consecutive numbers.\n\n**Derived values rebuilt automatically:**\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>` in `AssignMembershipNumber.java`) is built directly from `getCustomerCode()`, so it now carries the city-prefixed code with no logic change \u2014 I only updated its javadoc example.\n\n**Docs updated:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` schema descriptions and examples (`SYD-SMI-0007`, `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`).\n- Javadoc on both function classes.\n\nAll 26 tests (including the new `Cp09`/`Cp14`/`Cp16` customer-code tests) are green.",
